{
  "title": "Pangea™ Distal Anterolateral Tibia Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423208/pangea-tm--distal-anterolateral-tibia-plate",
  "subtitle": "Tibial Shaft Fractures Updated: Jun 8 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 distal tibia plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Distal Anterolateral Tibia (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Medial Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Posterior Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive plate-screw interface in the plate's locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423208/images/625c6801-c33e-4f31-983b-bb1fd0ebd1ed_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.26.54_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept nonlocking screws, and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**1.6mm K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Kickstand Screw**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Facilitates fixation of the posteromedial fragment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.7mm Distal Row**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Accepts variable angle locking screws, allowing for a low profile plate fit to reduce the potential for soft tissue irritation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423208/images/c24c8725-a6fa-495c-a8bd-4bb0a9ea2b90_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.26.45_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.7mm Screw**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Distal row allows for a low profile plate fit to reduce the potential for irritation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423208/images/c24c8725-a6fa-495c-a8bd-4bb0a9ea2b90_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.26.45_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This plate is placed on the anterolateral surface of the distal tibia",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Proper position is achieved when the distal end of the plate is adjacent to the articular surface, allowing for the distal screws to support the plafond",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Curvature of the Distal Anterolateral Tibia plates allow screw placement immediately proximal to the joint line for rafting while reducing the potential for soft tissue irritation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Shaft is anatomically curved proximally to the joint line for support distally, and designed to allow for a more centered placement of the distal screw cluster.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The Distal Anterolateral Tibia Plate provides better anatomic fit compared to competitive VA LCP distal anterolateral plates. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard anterolateral approach to the distal tibia. When using this approach, the superficial peroneal nerve is subcutaneous and must be protected",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard plate lengths: 3-18 hole (91-301mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: Shaft, 3.3mm, Distal 2.9mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T8: Ø2.0mm x 135mm (542000(S)) Ø2.0mm x 175mm (542001(S))",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T15: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Kickstand Screw",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Kickstand screw with a predetermined angle designed to assist with the fixxation of the posteromedial fragment. Variable angle option of the kickstand screw allows further reach for the fixxation of medial malleolus fragments.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
